  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound of {失|しつ} (lose) + {効|こう} (effect). Used as a suru verb ({失効|しっこう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧) to describe documents, contracts, or rights losing their validity.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {失効|しっこう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to expire, to lapse)\n- {失効|しっこう}{日|び} (expiration date)\n- {失効|しっこう}⟦した→する：00392_suru⟧⟦{免許|めんきょ}→免許：03808_menkyo⟧ (an expired license)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{期限切|きげんぎ}れ→期限切れ：15893_kigengire⟧: expiration — focuses on the deadline having passed\n- ⟦{無効|むこう}→無効：13385_mukou⟧: invalid — the state of not being valid, regardless of whether it once was",
